<hashTree>
<TestPlan guiclass="TestPlanGui" testclass="TestPlan" testname="QualityLab API performance">
  <stringProp name="TestPlan.comments">Performance test plan for the QualityLab REST API (/api/v1).
Settings come from JMeter properties: a target file (targets/*.properties) and a profile file (profiles/*.properties),
for example: jmeter -n -t plans/qualitylab-api.jmx -q targets/local.properties -q profiles/baseline.properties -l results.jtl -e -o dashboard
Credentials come from the TEST_USERNAME and TEST_PASSWORD environment variables (read by the setUp safety check).
Easiest: node scripts/run.js (see README.md).</stringProp>
  <boolProp name="TestPlan.functional_mode">false</boolProp>
  <boolProp name="TestPlan.tearDown_on_shutdown">true</boolProp>
  <boolProp name="TestPlan.serialize_threadgroups">false</boolProp>
  <elementProp name="TestPlan.user_defined_variables" elementType="Arguments" guiclass="ArgumentsPanel" testclass="Arguments" testname="User Defined Variables">
    <collectionProp name="Arguments.arguments"/>
  </elementProp>
</TestPlan>
